he user's seat wind is South Wind (F2), having a Pung of South Wind would give them 2 points. But since they only have one F2, playing it would prevent that. \n\nGiven that, perhaps playing B4 is better to keep the F2 for potential scoring. So the answer is Play B4.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Playing B4 allows forming a Chow of W6-W7-W8 and pairing B7, maximizing meld efficiency and maintaining potential for scoring patterns.  \nReason: Playing B4 retains F2 (South Wind, aligning with Seat Wind) for possible future scoring and enables a clean win with four melds and a pair.  \nAnswer: Play B4"}
