sed for a pair. Also, B7 is less likely to be needed by others compared to the terminals. So discarding one B7 would leave me with one B7, which can be part of a pair if I draw another. This could help in forming a Seven Pairs hand if I can get more pairs. Alternatively, it could be part of a Pung if I draw two more B7s, but that's a Kong.\n\nSo the best action is to Play B7.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The best move is to discard one of the B7 tiles to maximize potential for forming pairs or melds while minimizing risk to others.\nReason: Discarding B7 leaves a remaining B7 in hand, which can form a pair if another is drawn. This supports potential Seven Pairs or All Chows patterns. B7 is less likely to be critical for opponents compared to terminal tiles like W9 or T9. Keeping W7-8-9 intact preserves the possibility of forming a Chow, and discarding T2 or T9 might aid opponents with their existing melds.\nAnswer: Play B7"}
